feat(assets): ObjectData texture slots + glTF texture/material extraction

Step 4 (ObjectData expansion) and step 5a/5b (CPU-side texture and
material decode) from ENGINE_ROADMAP s 4.4. Visible change: none yet --
this is the data layout and CPU plumbing that the upcoming GPU upload +
normal-map sampling sits on top of.

Step 4 -- ObjectData 144 bytes:
- Added uvec4 textureIndices to ObjectData (baseColor / normal / MR /
  emissive bindless slots, 0xFFFFFFFF sentinel = no texture). Default
  member initializer hands the sentinel to every existing write site
  unchanged.
- static_assert(sizeof(ObjectData) == 144) on the C++ side, plus a
  must-match header comment on the eight shader copies (building /
  gbuffer / shadow / frustum_cull, each in GLSL and WGSL). The 2026-05-19
  shadow rewrite was caused by exactly this kind of stride drift, so the
  guard pays its rent.
- Old roughnessAOPad.b legacy bindless-albedo encoding stays in place
  during the transition; nothing reads textureIndices yet so the sentinel
  fill is dead storage, identical in shape to the tangent stream added in
  the previous commit.

Step 5a -- texture decode:
- AssetImporter decodes embedded glTF images. cgltf gives a
  cgltf_image*, and for glb files the bytes live in a buffer_view;
  decodeImage pulls the slice, hands it to stbi_load_from_memory with
  STBI_rgb_alpha, and stores RGBA8 pixels in an ImportedTexture (with
  the source name preserved). External uri references are flagged as
  unsupported with a log line rather than silently zeroed.

Step 5b -- material translation:
- ImportedMaterial now mirrors the glTF metallic-roughness model 1:1:
  baseColorFactor / metallicFactor / roughnessFactor / emissiveFactor /
  doubleSided plus the four texture indices, all resolved via pointer
  arithmetic on the cgltf textures array. KHR_materials_unlit, the
  specular-glossiness path, and KHR_materials extensions are deferred.

Build system:
- WASM build picks up stb via FetchContent against nothings/stb master,
  exposed as an INTERFACE target plus a Stb::stb ALIAS that matches the
  vcpkg name on native. ResourceManager.cpp still ifdef-guards the stb
  IMPLEMENTATION on WASM (no on-disk texture loads there), so the
  in-memory stbi_load_from_memory inside AssetImporter is the only WASM
  consumer of stb -- adding the dep was the missing piece.

Diagnostic log on a successful load now reads
  ingested N mesh(es), M primitive(s) skipped,
  K material(s), L texture(s) decoded (J skipped)
which is the cheapest end-to-end check that the extraction landed.

Both backends build clean. No rendering regression expected; the helmet
still shows as a neutral grey because no shader samples the new texture
data yet. GPU upload, the WebGPU material bind group, and normal-map
sampling land in subsequent commits.
